[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.AllDone.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum mumbles inaudibly.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆含混地低语，听不清楚。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Ascended.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum's countenance suddenly gravens.*}}\n\nO.. I know it to be arduous for you, meyvn, to see me like this. The imago unstrung... => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆的神情突然沉重起来。*}}\n\n哦……我知道，明识者，让你看见我这副模样很艰难。意象散线了……
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Ascended2.Text | I am sorry, =name=. I am so proud of you! I wish... I wish it were I did not peel, like your model. => 对不起，=name=。我真为你骄傲！我希望……我希望我没有像你的模型那样剥落。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Ascended3.Text | Farewell, now, meyvn. =name=. Live and drink. => 现在，告别了，明识者。=name=。生而饮水。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Ascended-No-Reveal.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum's countenance suddenly gravens.*}}\n\nChild. There is much more I would have liked to share. But... I am a puppet of my shame. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆的神情突然沉重起来。*}}\n\n孩子。我本还想分享更多。但……我是自己羞耻的傀儡。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Silent.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum mumbles inaudibly.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆含混地低语，听不清楚。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Hushed.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum weeps.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆哭泣。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Ascending.Text | We've-\n\nWe've done it, =name=. I- => 我们已经-\n\n我们做到了，=name=。我-
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.SortFaculties.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum exhales with effort.*}}\n\nLet us sort our faculties before we reach the rim of our ascent. There is the edge of our journey still to lathe. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆吃力地呼出一口气。*}}\n\n在我们到达攀升边缘前，先整理一下思绪吧。旅程还有最后一道边要打磨。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.TemplarDefeated.Text | I cannot say, =name=. But I know it's facile to believe a living heritage can be evanesced in one stroke. We are always downstream of a past violence. => 我说不准，=name=。但我知道，以为一种仍活着的遗产能一击抹掉，是太轻率了。过去的暴力总会流到我们这里。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Well.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum shifts his weight, pauses, and flexes an arthritic paw.*}}\n\nI am sorry. Tis the acceleration, =name=. I am whirling and empty of breath. Steel yourself, and so shall I. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆挪了挪重心，停顿片刻，屈伸着一只关节炎的爪子。*}}\n\n对不起。是加速度，=name=。我在旋转，喘不上气。你要坚强，我也会如此。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Awaits.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum pauses.*}}\n\nO, =name=, our cursors draw together on Fate's phenomenic slide rule! You burn with speculation, and I- I molder in the coolness of knowing. I enter my dwarf phase. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿。*}}\n\n哦，=name=，我们的游标在命运的现象滑尺上相互靠近！你因揣测而燃烧，而我- 我在知晓的冷意中腐朽。我进入了我的矮星相。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Awaits2.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum takes in a long breath.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆长长吸了一口气。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.NoMask.Text | I-\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum pauses, and then he laughs.*}}\n\nHo, ho! Still! The brow narrows in performance even as the play ends! The mask must peel off... What? No mask??\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum gravens suddenly.*}}\n\nI am sorry, =name=. I wish not to unnerve you with uncharacteristic lightness. You nor the rest deserve this. => 我-\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿，随后笑了起来。*}}\n\n呵，呵！仍是如此！即便戏已落幕，眉头仍在表演中收紧！面具必须剥下……什么？没有面具？？\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆突然沉重起来。*}}\n\n对不起，=name=。我不想用不合常态的轻快让你不安。你和其他人都不该承受这些。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.BarathrumRecovers.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum pauses.*}}\n\nForgive me, =name=. The ascent strains the mind as well as the body. My flight of fancy is done; I am regrounded. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿片刻。*}}\n\n原谅我，=name=。攀升不只折磨身体，也折磨心智。我已经不再胡思乱想，重新稳住了。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.BarathrumCusp.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum pauses and frowns.*}}\n\nDo you know, =name=, the engine types that ask us to loose every pin and unhinge every cam to know them? Such an engine of culture we are encased in now, and I cannot speak to the workings of one gearset without disassembling them all. I meant not to tease, and soon, I promise, you will spy the next arc of our journey. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿片刻，皱起眉头。*}}\n\n你知道吗，=name=，有些引擎必须松开每一枚销钉、拆下每一只凸轮，才能真正理解。我们现在就被包在这样一台文化引擎里；不把它全部拆开，我就说不清其中一组齿轮怎样运作。我不是有意吊你胃口。我保证，很快你就会看到我们旅程的下一段方向。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Reveal0.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum sighs.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆叹了口气。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Reveal1a.Text | You see, =name=, when I, a young bruin, crossed the Homs Delta with my flood-fleeing clan and into the western reach of Qud, the plagues of the Gyre were already ascendant. We took root at our new hearth, in the chrome grottos where we urshiib find natural peace, and by the providence of my elders, I was able to study the tinkering craft. => 你看，=name=，当年我还是一头年轻的熊，随躲洪水的氏族穿过霍姆斯三角洲，进入库德西境时，轮回诸疫已经兴起。我们在新的炉火旁扎根，在铬钢岩窟中安顿。那地方让我们乌尔希布天生感到平静；也多亏长辈许可，我得以学习修补技艺。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Reveal4.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum coughs and swallows.*}}\n\nTo ready our world for the Coven's return, the Seraph, who would be called Resheph, became convinced that all higher life on the planet must... be purged. That it was our life and way of living that moved the Coven to set the injunction. The only way through was for a new life to obtain. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆咳嗽，吞咽了一下。*}}\n\n为了让我们的世界为盟会归来做好准备，那位后来被称作瑞谢夫的炽天使确信，星球上一切高等生命都必须……被清除。他们认定，正是我们的生命和生活方式促使盟会降下禁令。唯一的出路，是让新的生命取得位置。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Reveal6.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum coughs and exhales a pained whistle.*}}\n\nTogether we beseeched Resheph, begged them to reverse the Gyre. I pleaded.. I-\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum wheezes.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆咳嗽，痛苦地呼出一声哨音。*}}\n\n我们一同恳求瑞谢夫，求他们逆转轮回。我哀求着……我——\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆喘息。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Rebekah.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum inhales and stutters.*}} She-\n\nResheph would not forgive her trespass. She contracted the rotting tongue while abetting the lepers of =RebekahRegion=. When her time came, she- => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆吸了一口气，结巴起来。*}} 她——\n\n瑞谢夫不愿宽恕她的越界。她在援助=RebekahRegion=的麻风病人时染上了腐舌病。等她的时候到了，她——
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Rebekah2.Text | Resheph would not let her return home. O..\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum expels a hushed whimper.*}} => 瑞谢夫不让她回家。噢……\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆发出一声压低的呜咽。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum whimpers.*}}\n\n-what? Who's there? => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆呜咽。*}}\n\n——什么？谁在那里？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed.Z-NameChoice.Text | It is me, Barathrum. =name=. => 是我，巴拉瑟姆。=name=。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Name.Text | Oh. Good, =name=, good... => 噢。好，=name=，好……
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed3.Text | In the late years I saw the writing on the wall. I turned us inward, retreated to my candle-dim study to angle at the project alone. A new plan... {{emote|*eeehw*}} was-\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum starts panting.*}} => 到了晚年，我已看见墙上的不祥字迹。我让我们转向内里，退回烛光昏暗的书房，独自斜着身子钻研这个计划。一个新计划……{{emote|*呃呜*}}本来是——\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆开始喘气。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed4.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum heaves a great sigh upon the moist air of the control pit.*}}\n{{emote|*Barathrum stumbles to the floor with paws to his face.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆在控制坑潮湿的空气中长长叹息。*}}\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆踉跄倒在地上，双爪捂住脸。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed5.Text | I failed it! I have failed! A thousand years too short, and- MORE TIME\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum weeps.*}} => 我搞砸了！我失败了！一千年太短，而且——更多时间\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆哭泣。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed8.Text | Then? Perhaps.. Perhaps the greater bodies whose agency I share the smaller cut from might share too the greater portion of my meal in blame.\n\nWinding Svy? Thou art devious in symbol shape like serpent Ba'al!\nHinnom? For blooming alga thou crossed thy perch's back!\nShiftless moon?\nSun! Proud and idle, Sun! Silver father of the protoplanets! Claim mine selfhood and be done with it.\n\n{{emote|*Barathrum weeps.*}} => 然后呢？也许……也许那些更大的躯体，我只从它们的行动性里分得一小份；它们也该替我的罪责分走更大一份。\n\n蜿蜒的斯维？你的符形狡猾得像蛇神巴力！\n欣嫩？为了盛开的藻，你越过了栖枝的脊背！\n飘忽的月亮？\n太阳！骄傲又闲散的太阳！原行星的白银之父！拿走我的自我，把一切了结吧。\n\n{{emote|*巴拉瑟姆哭泣。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-Failed9.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum weeps.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆哭泣。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-DotDotDot.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum weeps.*}} => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆哭泣。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-WhyAscend.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum's countenance suddenly burns bright.*}}\n\nDid you know, =name=, I harbor a memory older than even the flooding of my hearth cave. A gleaming ancient tale, told by my elders to the nippy cub I once was... => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆的神情忽然明亮起来。*}}\n\n你知道吗，=name=，我心中藏着一段记忆，比我炉洞被洪水淹没还要古老。那是一个闪光的古老传说，是长辈们讲给当年那个怕冷幼崽的……
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Z-WhyAscend2.Text | In the age of the covenate, a coterie of our urshiib ancestors took to the stars to ply their burning cores! Can you envision it??\n\nHo, ho! I know a secret! Heh, heh! I know... there is a functioning starship atop the Spindle. We can take it, =name=! We launch ourselves into the deepness of the dusted cosmos and find the starshiib! You and I, ho ho!\n\nStarshiib! => 在盟会时代，我们乌尔希布先祖中有一群同道奔赴群星，驱使他们燃烧的核心！你能想象吗？？\n\n呵，呵！我知道一个秘密！嘿，嘿！我知道……纺锤顶上有一艘还能运作的星舰。我们可以乘上它，=name=！我们把自己发射进积尘宇宙的深处，去寻找星希布！你和我，呵呵！\n\n星希布！
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Early.Text | Should you be here, =player.offspringTerm=? => =player.offspringTerm=，你应该在这里吗？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Recame.Text | Is that you, nestling =name=? Are you returned from gate and Tomb? Come closer, I say. => 是你吗，雏儿 =name=？你从门与陵墓归来了？靠近些，我说。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.PreKlanq.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum pauses.*}}\n\nIt is. For reasons I will explain shortly, for reasons beyond any of our remits, Klanq has returned to Grit Gate. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿片刻。*}}\n\n是。出于我稍后会解释的原因，也出于超出我们任何人权限的原因，克兰克回到了砂砾门。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.PreJunk.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum pauses.*}}\n\nUnusual circumstances have put my study in disarray. Lamentable, this is, but necessary. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿片刻。*}}\n\n异常局势让我的书房乱成一团。这令人惋惜，却也必要。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Brightsheol1.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum pauses.*}}\n\nI am confident there is a richness of wisdom in the poetry of that statement. One day, I will be eager to discover it. For now, what of the Spindle? => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆停顿片刻。*}}\n\n我确信那句话的诗意中蕴含着丰沛的智慧。总有一天，我会热切地去发现它。现在，纺锤如何了？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Brightsheol2.Text | {{emote|*Barathrum breathes a deep and relieved sigh.*}}\n\nYou are ever a courier of bright tidings, =name=. I am fond of this fact.\n\nCategories and types are decohering in these historic times. Nonetheless, the ritual nourishes us. You are raised to Meyvn, =name=. The one who understands. => {{emote|*巴拉瑟姆长长地、释然地叹了一口气。*}}\n\n你总是光明消息的信使，=name=。我很喜欢这一点。\n\n在这历史性的时代，范畴与类型正在退相干。尽管如此，仪式仍滋养我们。你被提升为明识者，=name=。那理解之人。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Golem3.Text | A new creature struggles to be born, =name=, and you will help birth it. Then, it will carry us, you and I, to the top of the Spindle. => 一个新生物正在挣扎着诞生，=name=，而你将帮助它出生。之后，它会载着你我登上纺锤之巅。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.AcceptGolem.Text | Yes, =name=! Begin the gathering, and the molding will follow. The materials you choose will influence the being we create, but any such being will be suitable for ascent.\n\nThis is our last task before we make our historic climb, =name=. Be safe and well in doing it. If you have more questions, return here. Klanq and I will be available. => 是的，=name=！开始收集吧，之后我们会进行塑形。你选的材料会影响我们创造出的存在，但不管最后是什么样，它都适合攀升。\n\n这是我们历史性攀登前的最后一项任务，=name=。办这件事时务必小心，愿你顺利。如果你还有问题，就回到这里。克兰克和我都会在。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.GolemQuestDone.Text | The creature is born, and you are bonded? What work! You are a sterling shaper of world, =name=, and I've nothing left to give you but my praise. => 生物已经诞生，而你也和它结合了？做得太好了！你是一位出色的世界塑形者，=name=，我已经没什么能给你，只剩下赞美。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Ascend.Text | Are you sure, Meyvn =name=? Our fates are not reversible past the next event horizon. => 你确定吗，明识者 =name=？一旦越过下一个事件视界，我们的命运就无法回头了。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.TombComplete.Text | You look... refreshed. Thank you, =name=. Take this polygel we recently recovered from the Palladium Reef. => 你看起来……焕然一新。谢谢你，=name=。收下这份多凝胶吧，是我们最近从钯礁寻回的。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.PaxComplete.Text | What welcome news, =factionaddress:Barathrumites=! Please, take this as a token of my gratitude. => 多么令人欣慰的消息，=factionaddress:Barathrumites=！请收下这个，作为我谢意的象征。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.TombBody2.Text | Strange, this, and imprecise, but as tinkers we know: a crude blueprint is better than no blueprint. You must return to Omonporch and enter the Tomb of the Eaters. Once inside, trace the errant paths cut into the mausoleum by robbers and vandals, and ascend to Resheph's burial chamber.\n\nAs for gaining entrance to the Tomb, Resheph sealed the gates a thousand years ago, but there's a flaw in the seal. The ancient Mark of Death has been lost to time, but if you were to recover it and incise the mark on your body, the Death Gate would open for you, as it did for countless Eater cadavers in the long-blurred past.\n\nRecover the Mark of Death, =name=, enter the Tomb, and cross into Brightsheol. Place your paws once again on the dial and drum. => 这说法很怪，也不够精确，但作为修补匠，我们知道：粗糙的蓝图总好过没有蓝图。你必须回到奥蒙廊，进入食客陵墓。进去后，沿着盗墓者与破坏者在陵墓中开出的岔路前行，升到瑞谢夫的墓室。\n\n至于怎么进入陵墓，瑞谢夫一千年前封住了大门，但封印有个破绽。古老的死亡印记已经失落在时间里，但如果你能找回它，并把印记刻在身上，死亡之门就会为你打开，就像它在久远模糊的过去曾为无数食客尸身打开一样。\n\n找回死亡印记，=name=，进入陵墓，穿入明灼阴府。让你的爪子再次按上旋钮与鼓面。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.TombBody3.Text | As I'd hoped you would, =name=. Take this disk with the signal encoded, just in case. And take this tattoo gun for when you recover the Mark of Death. You'll want to bring a pickaxe, too, or some other instrument for digging through stone. And beware: the Tomb is a vast and ancient space, and sacred to many. I cannot speak to what you will experience there. => 正如我所希望的，=name=。收下这张写入了信号的磁盘，以防万一。再收下这把纹身枪，等你取得死亡印记时会用到。最好也带上一把鹤嘴锄，或其他能挖穿石头的工具。还有，小心：陵墓是一片广阔而古老的空间，对许多人而言神圣不可侵犯。我说不准你在那里会经历什么。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.TombExplain2.Text | Strange, this, and imprecise, but as tinkers we know: a crude blueprint is better than no blueprint. You must return to Omonporch and enter the Tomb of the Eaters. Once inside, trace the errant paths cut into the mausoleum by robbers and vandals, and ascend to Resheph's burial chamber.\n\nAs for gaining entrance to the Tomb, Resheph sealed the gates a thousand years ago, but there's a flaw in the seal. The ancient Mark of Death has been lost to time, but if you were to recover it and incise the mark on your body, the Death Gate would open for you, as it did for countless Eater cadavers in the long-blurred past.\n\nYou're to recover the Mark of Death, =name=, enter the Tomb, and cross into Brightsheol. => 这说法很怪，也不够精确，但作为修补匠，我们知道：粗糙的蓝图总好过没有蓝图。你必须回到奥蒙廊，进入食客陵墓。进去后，沿着盗墓者与破坏者在陵墓中开出的岔路前行，升到瑞谢夫的墓室。\n\n至于怎么进入陵墓，瑞谢夫一千年前封住了大门，但封印有个破绽。古老的死亡印记已经失落在时间里，但如果你能找回它，并把印记刻在身上，死亡之门就会为你打开，就像它在久远模糊的过去曾为无数食客尸身打开一样。\n\n你要找回死亡印记，=name=，进入陵墓，穿入明灼阴府。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Quest.Text | I do. Your service to the guild has been laudable, =factionaddress:Barathrumites=. You braved the vaporous depths of Bethesda Susa and decoded the signal, you secured the Spindlegrounds and handled the self-appointed Earl, and perhaps most materially, you defended our enclave from the Putus Templar.\n\nSince you returned from Bethesda, you've no doubt wondered at the signal's contents. Verily, I hid them to shield you from the weight of the truth. Only Otho, Q Girl, and I bear that burden, but circumstances have changed. The river of Time powers the gear train of our schemes and devices, and it rushes forth. From here, I must share the burden. You must know. => 确实如此。你为行会做出的贡献值得称道，=factionaddress:Barathrumites=。你勇闯贝塞斯达苏萨雾汽弥漫的深处并解码了信号，你稳住了纺锤地并处理了那个自封伯爵，而也许最实质的是，你从普图斯圣殿骑士手中保卫了我们的飞地。\n\n自你从贝塞斯达归来后，无疑一直在猜想信号的内容。确实，我隐瞒了它们，是为了让你免受真相之重。只有奥索、Q 女孩和我承受着那份重担，但情势已变。时间之河驱动着我们计划与装置的齿轮组，并奔涌向前。从此刻起，我必须分担这重负。你必须知道。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.WhatNow.Text | I intend to ascend the Spindle and answer the call, =factionaddress:Barathrumites=.\n\nMy protege {{m|Q Girl}} has designed a climber for the ascent. We intended to construct it piecewise at the enclave and the site itself, but the engineering feat exceeds even our capacity. With time, I am confident we could accomplish it, but the Putus Templar rob us of our patience. We need to act now, and so as loath as I am to admit it, we need Pax Klanq. => 我打算攀上纺锤，回应那道呼唤，=factionaddress:Barathrumites=。\n\n我的门生 {{m|Q Girl}} 已经为攀升设计了一台攀升器。我们原本打算在飞地和现场分段建造它，但这项工程壮举甚至超出了我们的能力。若有时间，我相信我们能完成，可普图斯圣殿骑士夺走了我们的耐心。我们现在就必须行动，所以尽管我不愿承认，我们需要帕克斯·克兰克。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Barathrum.Accept.Text | As I had hoped, =factionaddress:Barathrumites=. First, speak with Q Girl. She'll hand over her design.\n\nI await your return. => 正如我所希望的，=factionaddress:Barathrumites=。首先，去和 Q 女孩谈谈。她会把设计交给你。\n\n我等你回来。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Resheph.WhyHere.EndChoice.Text | {{emote|*Tremble in fear.*}} => {{emote|*因恐惧而颤抖。*}}
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Resheph.Wakes6.NameChoice.Text | I am =name=. => 我是 =name=。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Covenant2.Text | When it began, =name= had no shared helices with the Reshephs previous, making their name through works and alliances alone. The lives taken and saved by =name= were myriad, uncountable, and only partially made record. Even Nephilim, once plagues of Qud, fell before the hand of =name=.\n\nAt the end of their reign, =name= called for peace with the surviving Nephilim and climbed to the top of the spire, there to end the Reshephate altogether and never be heard from again. => 一切开始时，=name= 与此前的瑞谢夫们并无共同螺旋，只凭事功与联盟赢得名号。被 =name= 夺走和拯救的生命数不胜数、无法计量，也只有一部分被记录下来。即便是曾为库德瘟疫的拿非利，也倒在 =name= 手下。\n\n在其统治的末尾，=name= 号召与幸存的拿非利和平共处，并登上尖塔之顶，在那里彻底终结瑞谢夫政权，从此再无音讯。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Covenant3.Text | Word of =name='s deeds reached record only after the unheralded appearance of the Knights Liminal, and broad assumption suggests that the former established the latter. It could be that the ancient Resheph yet lives within or outside of the boundaries of the Limen, but no word escapes its borders. => =name= 的事迹是在阈境骑士无预兆现身之后才进入记录；普遍推测认为前者创建了后者。那位古老瑞谢夫或许仍活在阈境边界内，或边界外，但没有任何消息能逃离其疆界。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Covenant3.CovenantPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Return2.Text | When their works began, =name= had no connection to the Sultanate. The rule of these ancient leaders had ended, but not fully: a ghost of the last Sultan yet ruled over the spire, tormenting those on and under the ground with plagues. As =name= grew mighty and slew the rampaging Nephilim, they came to recognize the source of their shared conflict.\n\nSeeking freedom from its reign, =name= struck a compact with the surviving Nephilim and climbed to the top of the spire, there to confront and banish the cerulean ghost.\n\nAnd so it proceeded. => 一切开始时，=name= 与苏丹国并无关系。这些古代领袖的统治已经终结，却并未完全终结：最后一位苏丹的幽灵仍统治着尖塔，以瘟疫折磨地上与地下的人。随着 =name= 日渐强大，斩杀横行的拿非利，他们逐渐认清了共同冲突的源头。\n\n为了摆脱其统治，=name= 与幸存的拿非利订立契约，并登上尖塔之顶，在那里直面并放逐那蔚蓝幽灵。\n\n于是事态便如此推进。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Return3.Text | Upon their return, =name= participated in the dissolution and federation of all power-concentrate. Allies of the new equalizer gathered and rose, forming the Quetzal Council and other, shorter-lived managing bodies.\n\nSince then, we have lived in tenuous harmony on the dwindling land and under it. => =name= 归来后，参与了所有权力集中体的解散与联邦化。新平权者的盟友聚集并崛起，组成羽蛇议会，以及其他存续较短的管理机构。\n\n自那以后，我们就在不断缩减的土地上与其下方，维持着脆弱的和谐。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Return3.ReturnPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Starfarer Story.Text | It begins in a time before =name='s ascension, when the spire rose unchallenged and unascended. The hollowers who committed their work to emptying our world were long gone, but long had rulers laid claim to the baffled ground in their place. Even as their holdings withered, they held on.\n\nBy the end of the time of Kings and Sultans, little remained of their works, less of their glory. => 故事始于 =name= 升攀之前，那时尖塔高耸，无人挑战，也无人攀登。那些献身于掏空我们世界的掏空者早已离去，但统治者们长久以来取而代之，宣称拥有那片令人困惑的大地。即便他们的领地日渐枯萎，他们仍紧握不放。\n\n到国王与苏丹的时代末尾，他们的事业已所剩无几，荣耀更少。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Starfarer2.Text | When it began, =name= had no shared helices with Qud's leaders, making their name through works and alliances alone. The lives taken and saved by =name= were myriad, uncountable, and only partially made record. Even Nephilim, once plagues of Qud, fell before the hand of =name=.\n\nAt the end of their reign, =name= called for peace with the surviving Nephilim and climbed to the top of the spire, there to quiet the ghosts of the Sultanate and take to the stars. => 一切开始时，=name= 与库德的领袖们并无共同螺旋，只凭事功与联盟赢得名号。被 =name= 夺走和拯救的生命数不胜数、无法计量，也只有一部分被记录下来。即便是曾为库德瘟疫的拿非利，也倒在 =name= 手下。\n\n在其统治的末尾，=name= 号召与幸存的拿非利和平共处，并登上尖塔之顶，在那里平息苏丹国的幽灵，奔向群星。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Starfarer3.Text | For centuries, we of listening inclination have kept sharp for some sign that =name= will return to the stars. Those of preaching inclination proclaim the imminent return of the starfarer, bearing tidings from parsecs forgotten and the last light of dying stars.\n\nAll others have lived in tenuous harmony on the dwindling land and under it, waiting for the next great history. => 数个世纪以来，我们这些倾向聆听者一直保持警觉，等待 =name= 将从群星归来的某种迹象。那些倾向布道者宣告星际远行者即将回返，带来被遗忘秒差距之外的消息，以及垂死恒星的最后光芒。\n\n其他所有人则在不断缩减的土地上与其下方，维持着脆弱的和谐，等待下一段伟大历史。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Starfarer3.StarfarerPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.StarfarerPC.Text | Who, indeed? Who ever was =name=? Dare we hang such hopes and fears on so tiny and distant a figure? Will it bear the weight? => 确实，谁呢？=name= 曾经究竟是谁？我们敢把这样的希望与恐惧悬挂在如此渺小又遥远的身影上吗？它承受得住这重量吗？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.StarfarerNephilim.Text | Their descendants remain and thrive, but the progenitor Nephilim have been silent for some time. Some believe that they have followed =name= to the stars. => 他们的后裔仍在，并且繁盛，但祖代拿非利已有一段时间沉默无声。有人相信他们已经追随 =name= 奔向群星。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Accession Story.Text | It begins in a time before the dread ascension of =name=, a time wherein the spire rose unchallenged and unascended. The hollowers who committed their work to emptying our world were long gone, but long had rulers laid claim to the baffled ground in their place. Even as their holdings withered, they held on.\n\nThe last of them would be the worst. => 故事始于 =name= 可怖升攀之前，那时尖塔高耸，无人挑战，也无人攀登。那些献身于掏空我们世界的掏空者早已离去，但统治者们长久以来取而代之，宣称拥有那片令人困惑的大地。即便他们的领地日渐枯萎，他们仍紧握不放。\n\n而他们中最后的那个，将会是最糟的。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Accession2.Text | When it began, =name= had no shared helices with Qud's leaders, making their name through the spilling of blood and terror. Uncountable lives were taken by their hand alone, all to slake age-old desires of control and might. Even the ancient plagueborn Nephilim fell before the hand of =name=.\n\nAt the end of their reign, =name= coerced a false compact with the surviving Nephilim and climbed to the top of the spire, the last remaining seat of the Sultanate's power. There, by one means or another, they sealed the fate of the world below.\n\nThe Plagues of the Gyre raged. Death swept Qud. => 一切开始时，=name= 与库德的领袖们并无共同螺旋，而是通过洒血与恐怖赢得名号。仅由其手夺走的生命便不可计数，全都用于满足对控制与强权的古老欲望。即便古老的疫生拿非利，也倒在 =name= 手下。\n\n在其统治的末尾，=name= 胁迫幸存的拿非利订立虚假契约，并登上尖塔之顶，那里是苏丹国权力最后残存的席位。在那里，他们以某种方式封定了下方世界的命运。\n\n轮回诸疫肆虐。死亡席卷库德。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Accession3.Text | In time, animal and even plant rule waned as their numbers fell to disease, slaughter, and wasting. More resilient, simple life took up the complexity left behind by the former rulers of Qud.\n\nWhat few Nervous Ones remained passed our stories on to the new life that saw fit to seek our counsel, that you remember the collective fate of those gone. Will you have your own =name=, or have you evolved truly past those before? => 随着时间推移，动物乃至植物的统治都衰退了，因为它们的数量在疾病、屠杀与消耗中下降。更有韧性的简单生命接过了库德昔日统治者留下的复杂性。\n\n所剩无几的神经者把我们的故事传给愿意寻求我们建议的新生命，让你们记住逝者的共同命运。你们也会拥有自己的 =name= 吗，还是你们真的已经进化越过了从前那些存在？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.Accession3.AccessionPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation PartialGodling.AccessionPC.Text | Who, indeed? Who ever was =name=? Dare we hang such hopes and fears on so tiny and distant a figure? Will it bear the weight? => 确实，谁呢？=name= 曾经究竟是谁？我们敢把这样的希望与恐惧悬挂在如此渺小又遥远的身影上吗？它承受得住这重量吗？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Covenant2.Text | When it began, =name= had no shared helices with the Reshephs previous, making their name through works and alliances alone. The lives saved and otherwise changed by =name= were myriad, uncountable, and only partially made record. When they spoke, even the plagues of Qud listened.\n\nAt the end of their reign, =name= made a compact with the Nephilim that they should never vex the creatures of Qud again. So done, they climbed to the top of the spire, there to end the Reshephate altogether and never be heard from again. => 一切开始时，=name= 与此前的瑞谢夫们并无共同螺旋，只凭事功与联盟赢得名号。被 =name= 拯救或以其他方式改变的生命数不胜数、无法计量，也只有一部分被记录下来。当他们开口时，连库德的瘟疫也会聆听。\n\n在其统治的末尾，=name= 与拿非利订立契约，令他们永不再侵扰库德的生灵。事成之后，他们登上尖塔之顶，在那里彻底终结瑞谢夫政权，从此再无音讯。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Covenant3.Text | Word of =name='s deeds reached record only after the unheralded appearance of the Knights Liminal, and broad assumption suggests that the former established the latter. It could be that the ancient Resheph yet lives within or outside of the boundaries of the Limen, but no word escapes its borders. => =name= 的事迹是在阈境骑士无预兆现身之后才进入记录；普遍推测认为前者创建了后者。那位古老瑞谢夫或许仍活在阈境边界内，或边界外，但没有任何消息能逃离其疆界。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Covenant3.CovenantPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Return2.Text | When their works began, =name= had no connection to the Sultanate. The rule of these ancient leaders had ended, but not fully: a ghost of the last Sultan yet ruled over the spire, tormenting those on and under the ground with plagues. As =name= grew mighty and challenged the rampaging Nephilim, they came to recognize the source of their shared conflict.\n\nSeeking freedom from the reign of the Sultan, =name= struck a compact with the Nephilim and climbed to the top of the spire, there to confront and banish the cerulean ghost.\n\nAnd so it proceeded. => 一切开始时，=name= 与苏丹国并无关系。这些古代领袖的统治已经终结，却并未完全终结：最后一位苏丹的幽灵仍统治着尖塔，以瘟疫折磨地上与地下的人。随着 =name= 日渐强大，挑战横行的拿非利，他们逐渐认清了共同冲突的源头。\n\n为了摆脱苏丹的统治，=name= 与拿非利订立契约，并登上尖塔之顶，在那里直面并放逐那蔚蓝幽灵。\n\n于是事态便如此推进。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Return3.Text | Upon their return, =name= participated in the dissolution and federation of all power-concentrate. Allies of the new equalizer gathered and rose, forming the Quetzal Council and other, shorter-lived managing bodies.\n\nSince then, we have lived in tenuous harmony on the dwindling land and under it. => =name= 归来后，参与了所有权力集中体的解散与联邦化。新平权者的盟友聚集并崛起，组成羽蛇议会，以及其他存续较短的管理机构。\n\n自那以后，我们就在不断缩减的土地上与其下方，维持着脆弱的和谐。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Return3.ReturnPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Starfarer Story.Text | It begins in a time before =name='s ascension, when the spire rose unchallenged and unascended. The hollowers who committed their work to emptying our world were long gone, but long had rulers laid claim to the baffled ground in their place. Even as their holdings withered, they held on.\n\nBy the end of the time of Kings and Sultans, little remained of their works, less of their glory. => 故事始于 =name= 升攀之前，那时尖塔高耸，无人挑战，也无人攀登。那些献身于掏空我们世界的掏空者早已离去，但统治者们长久以来取而代之，宣称拥有那片令人困惑的大地。即便他们的领地日渐枯萎，他们仍紧握不放。\n\n到国王与苏丹的时代末尾，他们的事业已所剩无几，荣耀更少。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Starfarer2.Text | When it began, =name= had no shared helices with Qud's leaders, making their name through works and alliances alone. The lives taken and saved by =name= were myriad, uncountable, and only partially made record. When they spoke, even the plagues of Qud listened.\n\nAt the end of their reign, =name= made a compact with the Nephilim that they should never vex the creatures of Qud again. So done, they climbed to the top of the spire and boarded an ancient vessel, thereby to travel the star-dusted expanse. => 一切开始时，=name= 与库德的领袖们并无共同螺旋，只凭事功与联盟赢得名号。被 =name= 夺走和拯救的生命数不胜数、无法计量，也只有一部分被记录下来。当他们开口时，连库德的瘟疫也会聆听。\n\n在其统治的末尾，=name= 与拿非利订立契约，令他们永不再侵扰库德的生灵。事成之后，他们登上尖塔之顶，登上一艘古老船只，由此前往星尘弥漫的广袤之域。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Starfarer3.Text | For centuries, we of listening inclination have kept sharp for some sign that =name= will return to the stars. Those of preaching inclination proclaim the imminent return of the starfarer, bearing tidings from parsecs forgotten and the last light of dying stars.\n\nAll others have lived in tenuous harmony on the dwindling land and under it, waiting for the next great history. => 数个世纪以来，我们这些倾向聆听者一直保持警觉，等待 =name= 将从群星归来的某种迹象。那些倾向布道者宣告星际远行者即将回返，带来被遗忘秒差距之外的消息，以及垂死恒星的最后光芒。\n\n其他所有人则在不断缩减的土地上与其下方，维持着脆弱的和谐，等待下一段伟大历史。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Starfarer3.StarfarerPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.StarfarerPC.Text | Who, indeed? Who ever was =name=? Dare we hang such hopes and fears on so tiny and distant a figure? Will it bear the weight? => 确实，谁呢？=name= 曾经究竟是谁？我们敢把这样的希望与恐惧悬挂在如此渺小又遥远的身影上吗？它承受得住这重量吗？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.StarfarerNephilim.Text | They lived.\n\nSimply a part of the world now, no longer a cilice scourging the Earth, they lived as the creatures they were. Descendants of their offspring walk on and under Qud. It's said that they ascended to the stars to find =name=, but it seems equally plausible that they may have returned to their slumber in the depths. => 他们活了下来。\n\n如今他们只是世界的一部分，不再是鞭笞大地的苦修刺衣；他们以自身生物的样子活着。他们子嗣的后代行走在库德地上与地下。据说他们升上群星去寻找 =name=，但同样可能的是，他们已回到深处沉眠。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Accession Story.Text | It begins in a time before the dread ascension of =name=, a time wherein the spire rose unchallenged and unascended. The hollowers who committed their work to emptying our world were long gone, but long had rulers laid claim to the baffled ground in their place. Even as their holdings withered, they held on.\n\nThe last of them would be the worst. => 故事始于 =name= 可怖升攀之前，那时尖塔高耸，无人挑战，也无人攀登。那些献身于掏空我们世界的掏空者早已离去，但统治者们长久以来取而代之，宣称拥有那片令人困惑的大地。即便他们的领地日渐枯萎，他们仍紧握不放。\n\n而他们中最后的那个，将会是最糟的。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Accession2.Text | When it began, =name= had no shared helices with Qud's leaders, making their name through the spilling of blood and terror. Uncountable lives were taken by their hand alone, all to slake age-old desires of control and might.\n\nPerhaps hunger turned to malice, or the adoption of a greater principle, or simple boredom. Whatever the reason, =name= formed a fast alliance with the ancient plagueborn Nephilim, ascended the spire, and sealed the fate of the world below.\n\nThe Plagues of the Gyre raged unchecked. => 一切开始时，=name= 与库德的领袖们并无共同螺旋，而是通过洒血与恐怖赢得名号。仅由其手夺走的生命便不可计数，全都用于满足对控制与强权的古老欲望。\n\n也许饥饿转为恶意，也许他们采纳了某种更大的原则，也许只是单纯无聊。不论原因如何，=name= 与古老的疫生拿非利迅速结盟，登上尖塔，封定了下方世界的命运。\n\n轮回诸疫不受遏制地肆虐。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Accession3.Text | In time, animal and even plant rule waned as their numbers fell to disease, slaughter, and wasting. More resilient, simple life took up the complexity left behind by the former rulers of Qud.\n\nWhat few Nervous Ones remained passed our stories on to the new life that saw fit to seek our counsel, that you remember the collective fate of those gone. Will you have your own =name=, or have you evolved truly past those before? => 随着时间推移，动物乃至植物的统治都衰退了，因为它们的数量在疾病、屠杀与消耗中下降。更有韧性的简单生命接过了库德昔日统治者留下的复杂性。\n\n所剩无几的神经者把我们的故事传给愿意寻求我们建议的新生命，让你们记住逝者的共同命运。你们也会拥有自己的 =name= 吗，还是你们真的已经进化越过了从前那些存在？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.Accession3.AccessionPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.AccessionPC.Text | Who, indeed? Who ever was =name=? Dare we hang such hopes and fears on so tiny and distant a figure? Will it bear the weight? => 确实，谁呢？=name= 曾经究竟是谁？我们敢把这样的希望与恐惧悬挂在如此渺小又遥远的身影上吗？它承受得住这重量吗？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation InheritorGodling.AccessionNephilim.Text | They played their role so well, and lived in power for a time.\n\nIf they had any illusion that they would be spared the fate =name= determined for life on Qud, it surely died before the great beings themselves. Mayhap they went to ground and survived. Mayhap their spawn persisted. => 他们很好地扮演了自己的角色，并一度活在权力之中。\n\n如果他们曾幻想自己能逃过 =name= 为库德生命定下的命运，那幻象必定早于这些伟大存在本身而死。也许他们遁入地下并幸存了。也许他们的子嗣延续了下来。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Covenant2.Text | None hailed =name=\nand =name= hailed none\nbut with word and blade\ndeed and disregard\nthey stood apart and above\n\nTo push back the Gyre,\nto spill of Nephil ichor\nthey took to the spire\nand quieted the Reshephate. => 无人向 =name= 致意\n=name= 也不向任何人致意\n但凭言语与刀锋\n行动与漠视\n他们卓然而立，高居其上\n\n为推退轮回，\n为洒出拿非利灵液\n他们登上尖塔\n平息了瑞谢夫政权。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Covenant3.CovenantPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.CovenantPC.Text | No one of fate,\nno one of blood,\nno one of importance,\nuntil, suddenly, someone of all of these things.\n\n=name= is a dream from which we cannot awaken. => 无命运之人，\n无血脉之人，\n无重要之人，\n直到忽然成为兼具这一切的人。\n\n=name= 是我们无法醒来的梦。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Return2.Text | None hailed =name=\nand =name= hailed none\nbut with word and blade\ndeed and disregard\nthey stood against old rule.\n\nTo push back the Gyre,\nto spill of Nephil ichor\nthey took to the spire\nand quieted the remnants. => 无人向 =name= 致意\n=name= 也不向任何人致意\n但凭言语与刀锋\n行动与漠视\n他们站出来反抗旧日统治。\n\n为推退轮回，\n为洒出拿非利灵液\n他们登上尖塔\n平息了残余者。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Return3.Text | Upon their return\nwhat power =name= wrested\nthey called on allies\nto distribute and dissolve.\n\nThe Freeholders,\nnew hollowers,\nthe Quetzal Council,\nand other such fools.\n\nCountless years of struggle\ncenturies of change.\nWe remember what we can\nand watch new and old die. => =name= 归来之时\n将夺来的权力\n召来盟友\n分配并消解。\n\n自由领民，\n新的掏空者，\n羽蛇议会，\n以及其他这样的愚者。\n\n无数年的斗争\n数个世纪的变迁。\n我们记住所能记住的\n看着新旧一同死去。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Return3.ReturnPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.ReturnPC.Text | No one of fate,\nno one of blood,\nno one of importance,\nuntil their return\nand the realization of their future.\n\n=name= is a temple in memory\nupon which hopes are hung\nand rage is borne out.\n\nToo great to be real,\ntoo foundational not to be,\ntoo contradictory to have ever existed. => 无命运之人，\n无血脉之人，\n无重要之人，\n直到他们归来\n直到他们的未来实现。\n\n=name= 是记忆中的一座神庙\n希望悬挂其上\n怒火由此承载而出。\n\n太伟大以至于不真实，\n太根本以至于不能不存在，\n太矛盾以至于不可能曾经存在。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Starfarer2.Text | None hailed =name=\nand =name= hailed none\nbut with word and blade\ndeed and disregard\nthey stood against old rule.\n\nTo push back the Gyre,\nto spill of Nephil ichor\nthey took to the spire\nand quieted the remnants. => 无人向 =name= 致意\n=name= 也不向任何人致意\n但凭言语与刀锋\n行动与漠视\n他们站出来反抗旧日统治。\n\n为推退轮回，\n为洒出拿非利灵液\n他们登上尖塔\n平息了残余者。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Starfarer3.Text | Though =name= was gone\nour memories remained\nand the plagues receded\nand many rejoiced.\n\nTo this day\neyes turn to the stars\nlooking for a sign that our starfarer\nhas deigned to return.\n\nCountless years of struggle\ncenturies of change.\nWe remember what we can\nand watch new and old die. => 虽然 =name= 离去了\n我们的记忆仍存\n瘟疫退却\n许多人欢欣。\n\n直到今日\n目光仍转向群星\n寻找我们的星际远行者\n屈尊归来的迹象。\n\n无数年的斗争\n数个世纪的变迁。\n我们记住所能记住的\n看着新旧一同死去。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Starfarer3.StarfarerPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.StarfarerPC.Text | Starfarer, herald, disruptor,\nfeared, revered,\nsavior and abandoner.\n\n=name= is a dream from which we will one day awaken. => 星际远行者，先驱，扰乱者，\n被恐惧，被敬畏，\n救世者，也是抛弃者。\n\n=name= 是我们终有一日会醒来的梦。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Accession2.Text | None hailed =name=\nand =name= hailed none\nbut with word and blade\ndeed and disregard\nthey stood against their kind.\n\nTo push back the Gyre,\nto spill of Nephil ichor\nthey took to the spire\nand enacted a great betrayal.\n\nDeath of impossible scale reigned\nand we Nervous Ones fell,\nand as the Gyre swallowed us\nwe sang to the last. => 无人向 =name= 致意\n=name= 也不向任何人致意\n但凭言语与刀锋\n行动与漠视\n他们站出来反抗同类。\n\n为推退轮回，\n为洒出拿非利灵液\n他们登上尖塔\n上演了一场伟大背叛。\n\n不可能规模的死亡统治一切\n我们神经者倒下，\n而当轮回吞没我们时\n我们歌唱到最后。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation Fool.Accession3.AccessionPCChoice.Text | Who is =name=? => =name= 是谁？
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation SpokenIonic.Ionic.Text | Gathered and spun, I emerge into {{zetachrome|Spoken Ionic Through Covalency Heart}}.\nWhat is... what are. I cannot.\nFinding no entry, for the rest is at home. A strand to you. => 聚集并旋成，我显现为 {{zetachrome|经共价心言说的离子}}。\n是什么……是什么们。我不能。\n找不到条目，因为其余在家中。一缕给你。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation SpokenIonic.Ionic.GreetChoice.Text | Greetings, Spoken Ionic Through Covalency Heart. I am =name=. => 你好，经共价心言说的离子。我是 =name=。
[QudCnSupplement] STRING_REVIEW: Conversation SpokenIonic.Others.Text | For temple 'here' yes:\n{{zetachrome|Spoken Ionic Through Covalency Heart}} here.\nAlso, you. => 若神庙“这里”，是：\n{{zetachrome|经共价心言说的离子}} 在这里。\n还有，你。
